## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to apply progressive hydration, per-column lazy-loading, and worker offloading to meet Lighthouse budgets in a heavy dashboard. Also probes SSR/CSR trade-offs and how to validate improvements.

## Key Concepts

- Progressive hydration
- Dynamic imports and code-splitting
- Virtualization
- Web Workers
- Lighthouse budgets and metrics
- IntersectionObserver for loading offscreen content

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example skeleton: dynamic import of heavy cell renderer
import dynamic from 'next/dynamic';
const HeavyCell = dynamic(() => import('./cells/HeavyCell'));

// Progressive hydration with IntersectionObserver
const useColumnHydration = (columnRef) => {
  const [isHydrated, setIsHydrated] = useState(false);

  useEffect(() => {
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
      ([entry]) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          setIsHydrated(true);
          observer.disconnect();
        }
      },
      { threshold: 0.1 }
    );

    if (columnRef.current) {
      observer.observe(columnRef.current);
    }

    return () => observer.disconnect();
  }, []);

  return isHydrated;
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to implement a small, practical caching layer with closures, per-URL keys, in-flight request sharing, and TTL-based invalidation using Promises. It mirrors common frontend API client patterns at scale.

## Key Concepts
- Closures to encapsulate cache state
- Per-URL Map storage with {promise, expires}
- Concurrency control: share in-flight Promise across callers
- TTL-based invalidation and error handling for retries
- fetch API and parsing JSON safely

## Code Example
```javascript
function makeApiClient() {
  const cache = new Map();
  return {
    fetchWithCache: (url, ttlMs) => {
      const now = Date.now();
      const entry = cache.get(url);
      if (entry && now < entry.expires) {
        return entry.promise;
      }
      const promise = fetch(url).then(res => {
        if (!res.ok) throw new Error(res.statusText || res.status);
        return res.json();
      }).catch(err => {
        cache.delete(url);
        throw err;
      });
      cache.set(url, { promise, expires: ttlMs != null ? now + ttlMs : Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY });
      return promise;
    }
  };
}
```

